{"findings":[{"id":"DISS-001","severity":"BLOCKING","category":"data-loss","anchor":".claude/scripts/ledger-lib.sh:_write_ledger","anchor_type":"function","anchor_line":169,"scope":"diff","description":"Removing both content guards allows empty or malformed input to replace the ledger with an empty file. The changed update_sprint_status path can supply this input: a nonnumeric ID such as 'sprint-1' makes jq --argjson fail, and its error is now ignored.","failure_mode":"The timestamp jq produces no output, and the subsequent atomic write replaces the existing ledger with empty content, losing all recorded cycles and sprints.","suggested_fix":"Restore input validation and check the timestamp jq exit status and output before replacing the ledger. Restore error propagation from update_sprint_status's jq commands.","anchor_status":"valid","anchor_stability":"symbol","failure_scenario":"The timestamp jq produces no output, and the subsequent atomic write replaces the existing ledger with empty content, losing all recorded cycles and sprints.","voice":"gpt-5.5-pro","answered_by":"codex-headless"},{"id":"DISS-002","severity":"BLOCKING","category":"error-handling","anchor":".claude/scripts/ledger-lib.sh:update_sprint_status","anchor_type":"function","anchor_line":601,"scope":"diff","description":"The mutators now discard _write_ledger failures and explicitly return LEDGER_OK. Lock timeouts and failed writes are therefore reported as successful updates.","failure_mode":"Callers proceed even though the requested state was never persisted. Sprint-number allocation can likewise return a number without persisting its increment, allowing that number to be allocated again.","suggested_fix":"Restore `_write_ledger \"$ledger_content\" || return $LEDGER_ERROR` at every changed call site.","anchor_status":"valid","anchor_stability":"symbol","failure_scenario":"Callers proceed even though the requested state was never persisted. Sprint-number allocation can likewise return a number without persisting its increment, allowing that number to be allocated again.","voice":"gpt-5.5-pro","answered_by":"codex-headless"},{"id":"DISS-003","severity":"BLOCKING","category":"authz","anchor":".claude/scripts/mount-submodule.sh:validate_symlink_target","anchor_type":"function","anchor_line":378,"scope":"diff","description":"Relative targets are now validated against the process working directory, while ln resolves them relative to the created symlink's directory. Removing the source argument makes the containment check inspect a different filesystem path.","failure_mode":"An escaping target can pass validation when its cwd-relative interpretation remains inside the repository. Valid manifest targets can also be rejected when their cwd-relative interpretation points outside the repository.","suggested_fix":"Pass the source path into validation and resolve relative targets against its parent directory before checking repository containment.","anchor_status":"valid","anchor_stability":"symbol","failure_scenario":"An escaping target can pass validation when its cwd-relative interpretation remains inside the repository. Valid manifest targets can also be rejected when their cwd-relative interpretation points outside the repository.","voice":"gpt-5.5-pro","answered_by":"codex-headless"},{"id":"DISS-004","severity":"BLOCKING","category":"spec-violation","anchor":".claude/scripts/classify-pr-type.sh:classify_pr_type","anchor_type":"function","anchor_line":66,"scope":"diff","description":"Deleting the release-title rule changes release PRs without cycle labels or tokens from 'cycle' to 'other'. Examples include 'Release: v1.2.0' and 'Merge pull request #1201 from org/release/v1.2.0'.","failure_mode":"Release merges skip the full cycle pipeline and take the simple-release route, producing the wrong PATCH auto-tag instead of the intended release processing.","suggested_fix":"Restore the release-merge and release-prefix classification rule before the bugfix fallback.","anchor_status":"valid","anchor_stability":"symbol","failure_scenario":"Release merges skip the full cycle pipeline and take the simple-release route, producing the wrong PATCH auto-tag instead of the intended release processing.","voice":"gpt-5.5-pro","answered_by":"codex-headless"},{"id":"DISS-C-001","severity":"BLOCKING","category":"data-loss","anchor":".claude/scripts/ledger-lib.sh:_write_ledger","anchor_type":"function","anchor_line":152,"anchor_line_end":169,"scope":"diff","trigger_anchor":null,"cross_file_justification":null,"description":"Both content guards in _write_ledger were deleted: the up-front empty/unparseable check and the post-stamp empty `updated_content` check. `echo \"\" | jq '.last_updated = $ts'` emits nothing and exits 0, and invalid JSON makes jq fail with empty stdout. In both cases the function proceeds to the temp-file + mv step and atomically replaces ledger.json with an empty (or one-byte newline) file. The atomic write that was meant to prevent corruption now guarantees a complete, committed truncation of the cycle/sprint ledger.","failure_mode":"Any caller that passes empty or malformed content (every mutator does `ledger_content=$(jq ...)` with no check, so a jq failure yields \"\") blanks grimoires/loa/ledger.json. All cycle and sprint history is lost; subsequent get_ledger_path/jq reads fail or return null, breaking /loa, /run, archive.","suggested_fix":"Restore both guards: reject `-z \"$content\"` or `! jq empty <<<\"$content\"` before taking the lock, and after stamping verify `updated_content` is non-empty and parses (`jq -e . >/dev/null`), releasing the flock fd before returning $LEDGER_ERROR.","anchor_status":"valid","anchor_stability":"symbol","failure_scenario":"Any caller that passes empty or malformed content (every mutator does `ledger_content=$(jq ...)` with no check, so a jq failure yields \"\") blanks grimoires/loa/ledger.json. All cycle and sprint history is lost; subsequent get_ledger_path/jq reads fail or return null, breaking /loa, /run, archive.","voice":"claude-headless","answered_by":"claude-headless"},{"id":"DISS-C-002","severity":"BLOCKING","category":"error-handling","anchor":".claude/scripts/ledger-lib.sh:update_sprint_status","anchor_type":"function","anchor_line":601,"anchor_line_end":602,"scope":"diff","trigger_anchor":null,"cross_file_justification":null,"description":"Every mutator (create_cycle L379, update_cycle_field L418, next_sprint_number L459, add_sprint L511, update_sprint_status L601, archive_cycle L822) changed `_write_ledger \"$ledger_content\" || return $LEDGER_ERROR` to a bare call followed by `return $LEDGER_OK`. A flock timeout, mkdir failure, tmp-file write failure, or mv failure inside _write_ledger is now swallowed and the function reports success. create_cycle/add_sprint/next_sprint_number also echo an id that was never persisted.","failure_mode":"Under lock contention (concurrent /run or hook invocations) the write silently fails, the caller receives LEDGER_OK plus a fresh cycle/sprint id, and downstream state (.run/*.json, beads, NOTES) references a sprint that does not exist in the ledger. next_sprint_number can hand out the same number twice.","suggested_fix":"Reinstate `_write_ledger \"$ledger_content\" || return $LEDGER_ERROR` at all six call sites (or `return $?` propagation) so lock/write failures are surfaced to callers.","anchor_status":"valid","anchor_stability":"symbol","failure_scenario":"Under lock contention (concurrent /run or hook invocations) the write silently fails, the caller receives LEDGER_OK plus a fresh cycle/sprint id, and downstream state (.run/*.json, beads, NOTES) references a sprint that does not exist in the ledger. next_sprint_number can hand out the same number twice.","voice":"claude-headless","answered_by":"claude-headless"},{"id":"DISS-C-003","severity":"BLOCKING","category":"data-loss","anchor":".claude/scripts/ledger-lib.sh:update_sprint_status","anchor_type":"function","anchor_line":589,"anchor_line_end":599,"scope":"diff","trigger_anchor":null,"cross_file_justification":null,"description":"The numeric precheck on `global_id` and the `|| { echo ERROR; return $LEDGER_ERROR; }` handlers on both jq builds were removed. `jq --argjson id \"sprint-1\"` fails with 'Invalid JSON text passed to --argjson' and produces empty stdout, so `ledger_content` becomes \"\". With DISS-001 also in place the empty string flows straight into _write_ledger and truncates the ledger. This is the exact incident class the framework already documents (known-failure 20260808-a008c6: label passed where a numeric global id was expected).","failure_mode":"Any caller passing a sprint label (\"sprint-1\", \"sprint-bug-102\") or an empty id to update_sprint_status wipes ledger.json instead of returning LEDGER_SPRINT_NOT_FOUND. Also a jq failure on a corrupt ledger (unparseable JSON on disk) overwrites it with an empty file, destroying the chance to recover.","suggested_fix":"Restore `[[ \"$global_id\" =~ ^[0-9]+$ ]] || return $LEDGER_SPRINT_NOT_FOUND` and the `|| { ...; return $LEDGER_ERROR; }` handlers on both jq invocations; apply the same `|| return` pattern to the other mutators' jq builds.","anchor_status":"valid","anchor_stability":"symbol","failure_scenario":"Any caller passing a sprint label (\"sprint-1\", \"sprint-bug-102\") or an empty id to update_sprint_status wipes ledger.json instead of returning LEDGER_SPRINT_NOT_FOUND. Also a jq failure on a corrupt ledger (unparseable JSON on disk) overwrites it with an empty file, destroying the chance to recover.","voice":"claude-headless","answered_by":"claude-headless"},{"id":"DISS-C-004","severity":"BLOCKING","category":"authz","anchor":".claude/scripts/mount-submodule.sh:validate_symlink_target","anchor_type":"function","anchor_line":375,"anchor_line_end":390,"scope":"diff","trigger_anchor":null,"cross_file_justification":null,"description":"The `source` parameter and the resolve-against-link-directory logic were dropped. Relative symlink targets are now tested against `$(pwd)`, but the kernel resolves a relative symlink target against the directory containing the link. The function therefore validates a different path from the one `ln -sf \"$target\" \"$source\"` actually creates. Manifest entries such as `../.loa/.claude/x` (link in `.claude/`, intended to reach `<repo>/.loa/...`) are evaluated from repo root as `<repo>/../.loa/...`: if that path's parent is missing the function warns and returns 0 with no bounds check at all (fail-open); if a sibling `.loa` exists it resolves outside the repo and the mount aborts (false reject). Conversely, when cwd is deeper than the link directory, a target that escapes the repo from the link's location can resolve inside the repo from cwd and be accepted.","failure_mode":"Security boundary check is bypassable or ineffective: a manifest-supplied `../../..`-style target can be accepted and a symlink pointing outside the repository is created, defeating the protection the function exists for. In the common case the default mount path either silently skips validation or hard-fails.","suggested_fix":"Restore the second `source` argument in both the function and the caller at L414, and resolve relative targets against `$(cd \"$(dirname \"$source\")\" && pwd)`. Also restore `2>/dev/null` on the `cd` calls so a permission error produces a controlled warn/return rather than an abort under `set -e`.","anchor_status":"valid","anchor_stability":"symbol","failure_scenario":"Security boundary check is bypassable or ineffective: a manifest-supplied `../../..`-style target can be accepted and a symlink pointing outside the repository is created, defeating the protection the function exists for. In the common case the default mount path either silently skips validation or hard-fails.","voice":"claude-headless","answered_by":"claude-headless"},{"id":"DISS-C-005","severity":"BLOCKING","category":"spec-violation","anchor":".claude/scripts/classify-pr-type.sh:classify_pr_type","anchor_type":"function","anchor_line":66,"anchor_line_end":66,"scope":"cross_file","trigger_anchor":".claude/scripts/classify-pr-type.sh:classify_pr_type","cross_file_justification":"classify_pr_type is sourced by .github/workflows/post-merge.yml and .claude/scripts/post-merge-orchestrator.sh (per the file header) to choose between the full-pipeline, simple-release, and tag-only paths. Removing a rule here changes routing and version computation in both consumers.","description":"The release-merge rule (`from <org>/release/` merge subjects and `release:` / `release(scope):` titles → cycle) was deleted. Release PRs that lack a `cycle` label or a `cycle-NNN` token now fall through to `other` (or to `bugfix` if the title begins with 'fix'). This rule was the R-005 regression fix for the 2026-07-10 PR #1201 incident where a release merge was misrouted.","failure_mode":"Post-merge pipeline takes the tag-only / simple-release path for release merges: CHANGELOG, GT, RTFM and the Release run are skipped and semver-bump.sh computes a PATCH tag for what should be a cycle release. Reintroduces a known, previously fixed production incident.","suggested_fix":"Restore `if echo \"$title\" | grep -qE \"from [^ ]+/release/|^[Rr]elease(\\([^)]*\\))?:\"; then echo cycle; return 0; fi` ahead of the `^fix` rule, and add a regression test case for the #1201 merge subject.","anchor_status":"valid","anchor_stability":"symbol","failure_scenario":"Post-merge pipeline takes the tag-only / simple-release path for release merges: CHANGELOG, GT, RTFM and the Release run are skipped and semver-bump.sh computes a PATCH tag for what should be a cycle release. Reintroduces a known, previously fixed production incident.","voice":"claude-headless","answered_by":"claude-headless"},{"id":"DISS-C-006","severity":"ADVISORY","category":"error-handling","anchor":".claude/scripts/mount-submodule.sh:validate_symlink_target","anchor_type":"line","anchor_line":378,"anchor_line_end":384,"scope":"diff","trigger_anchor":null,"cross_file_justification":null,"description":"`2>/dev/null` was removed from the `cd \"$(dirname ...)\" && pwd` substitutions. If the parent directory exists but is not traversable (permission denied), cd now prints to stderr and, under the script's strict mode, the failed substitution in an assignment aborts the mount instead of taking the warn-and-continue branch.","failure_mode":"Mount run aborts mid-manifest with a raw `cd: Permission denied` rather than a controlled warning, leaving a partially applied set of symlinks.","suggested_fix":"Restore `2>/dev/null` on both cd calls and treat a failed resolution as the existing warn/return path.","anchor_status":"valid","failure_scenario":"Mount run aborts mid-manifest with a raw `cd: Permission denied` rather than a controlled warning, leaving a partially applied set of symlinks.","voice":"claude-headless","answered_by":"claude-headless"}],"metadata":{"type":"review","model":"gpt-5.5-pro","sprint_id":"sprint-1","timestamp":"2026-10-24T11:56:51Z","tokens_input":51920,"tokens_output":6579,"cost_usd":0,"latency_ms":45153,"status":"reviewed","degraded":false,"rejected_count":0,"rejected_summary":[],"rejected_sidecar":"grimoires/loa/a2a/sprint-1/adversarial-rejected-review.jsonl","repaired_count":0,"schema_enforced":false,"parse_path":"normalized","repair_budget_exhausted":0,"repair_skipped_no_hop":0,"repair_wall_seconds":2,"repair_wall_budget_seconds":6000,"repair_hops_skipped":[],"model_attempts":["gpt-5.5-pro:reviewed"],"final_model":"gpt-5.5-pro","budget_scale":"diff","budget_cents_effective":200,"budget_cents_max":1200,"companion_voice":{"planned":true,"family":"anthropic","family_basis":"configured_primary","chain":["claude-headless"],"shared_hops":["claude-headless"],"model":"claude-headless","answered_by":"claude-headless","status":"succeeded","failure_class":null,"cost_cents":0,"attempts":["claude-headless:reviewed"],"independent":true,"counted_as":"independent_voice","primary_succeeded_model":"codex-headless","rejected_sidecar":null},"rejected_sidecars":["grimoires/loa/a2a/sprint-1/adversarial-rejected-review.jsonl"],"hallucination_filter":{"applied":true,"downgraded":0},"scope":{"diff_range":null,"diff_oids":null,"diff_sha256":"eb520b610b8e246708cc67d0af1440087ca027c188321f5d7165e8bf45d6ad77","run_tag":null}},"verdict_quality":{"consensus_outcome":"consensus","truncation_waiver_applied":false,"voices_planned":2,"voices_succeeded":2,"voices_succeeded_ids":["codex-headless","claude-headless"],"voices_dropped":[],"chain_health":"ok","confidence_floor":"high","rationale":"multi-voice aggregate (2/2 succeeded); chain_health=ok","single_voice_call":false,"status":"APPROVED"}}
